Design a circuit that implements a 7-bit binary adder with an additional carry out, allowing for 8-bit inputs. The module takes two 8-bit inputs and computes their sum, producing a 9-bit output that includes the carry from the most significant bit addition. The design uses a series of bitwise AND and XOR operations to generate partial products and propagate carry bits through the adder stages, enabling efficient summation while handling carry propagation for each bit addition.
