description:
Design a voltage level shifter that converts an n-bit input signal from a lower voltage level (v1 = 1.8V) to a higher voltage level (v2 = 3.3V) for m-bit output. The module processes each input bit and generates corresponding output signals based on the input's logical state, aiming to ensure interoperability between components operating at different voltage levels. The output consists of the most significant m bits of the transformed input signals.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output [m-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output [m-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of input signals
parameter m = 2; // number of output signals
parameter v1 = 1.8; // voltage level of the input signals
parameter v2 = 3.3; // voltage level of the output signals

// Voltage level shifter circuit
wire [n-1:0] shifted;
genvar i;
generate
  for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) begin : shifter
    assign shifted[i] = (in[i] == 1'b1) ? (v2 / v1) : 1'b0;
  end
endgenerate

// Connect the shifted signals to the output signals
assign out = shifted[m-1:0];

endmodule

