description:
Design a 3-to-8 line decoder that takes a 3-bit binary input and activates one of the eight output lines corresponding to the input value, while ensuring all other outputs are driven low. When the input value is 3'b000, the first output line is asserted, and this pattern continues such that each binary input activates the respective line, following a negative logic convention where active outputs are '0'. If the input is out of the 0-7 range, all outputs remain inactive (high).
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    output reg [7:0] out
);always @(*) begin
    case (in)
        3'b000: out = 8'b11111110;
        3'b001: out = 8'b11111101;
        3'b010: out = 8'b11111011;
        3'b011: out = 8'b11110111;
        3'b100: out = 8'b11101111;
        3'b101: out = 8'b11011111;
        3'b110: out = 8'b10111111;
        3'b111: out = 8'b01111111;
        default: out = 8'b11111111;
    endcase
end

endmodule

