description:
Design a priority encoder that takes an 8-bit input and outputs a 3-bit binary code corresponding to the highest-order active input bit. The output indicates the position of the most significant '1' bit in the input, with each position mapped to a specific output value. If no input bits are active, the output defaults to '000'.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] in,
  output reg [2:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] in,
  output reg [2:0] out
);always @* begin
    case(in)
      8'b10000000: out = 3'b000;
      8'b01000000: out = 3'b001;
      8'b00100000: out = 3'b010;
      8'b00010000: out = 3'b011;
      8'b00001000: out = 3'b100;
      8'b00000100: out = 3'b101;
      8'b00000010: out = 3'b110;
      8'b00000001: out = 3'b111;
      default: out = 3'b000;
    endcase
  end

endmodule

